# Media Pipeline and Workers

- Treat inference and rendering as resource-intensive background work.
- Bound CPU, GPU, RAM, disk, and worker concurrency; do not assume large models fit the development machine.
- Inspect model VRAM/RAM requirements and license before integration.
- Persist meaningful job states; make jobs resumable and idempotent where practical.
- Support cancellation, timeouts, bounded retries, and clear failure reasons.
- Cache reusable artifacts with stable content-based keys.
- Stream large files when possible; avoid loading entire media assets into memory.
- Validate duration, dimensions, codecs, and file size at upload and processing boundaries.
- Clean temporary files safely; do not delete user assets as part of generic cleanup.
- Keep provider/model adapters replaceable and isolate hardware-specific configuration.
- Use FFmpeg arguments safely; never interpolate untrusted input into shell commands.
- Test failure recovery, partial outputs, and concurrent job execution.
